      "en": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Happy are those who (wherever they are) are living in the house of Hashem (are living a meaningful and spiritually growing life); עוֹד יְהַלְלוּךָ סֶּלָה—they will constantly praise You (since they see all the circumstances of their life as opportunities for growth). אַשְׁרֵי הָעָם שֶׁכָּכָה לּוֹ—Happy and fortunate are we, the nation (Bnei Yisrael) that has all this (glorious history and great mission); אַשְׁרֵי הָעָם שֶׁיהֹוָה אֱלֹהָיו—happy and fortunate are we, the nation (Bnei Yisrael) that has Hashem as our personal God Who takes care of us."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 0
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "A song of praise by David HaMelech (תהילים קמה): אֲרוֹמִמְךָ אֱלוֹהַי הַמֶּלֶךְ—I will exalt and revere You (since I realize that the essence of Hashem as my personal God and Ruler of the entire universe is way beyond our human comprehension); וַאֲבָרְכָה שִׁמְךָ—and (at the same time) I thank You (in the following verses) for all that You have done and will do (for me personally and for our nation); לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד—since the beginning of time and until the end of days."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 2
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(You are the Source of everything that happens to me each and every day, and) I thank You for it all (even though some of those things are hard to understand); וַאֲהַלְלָה שִׁמְךָ לְעוֹלָם וָעֶד—and in the end of days, I will truly praise You (as all becomes clear)."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 3
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(As much as we will thank and praise Hashem, and proclaim) Hashem is \"great\" and is \"extremely praised\";"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 4
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(the truth is that) the greatness of Hashem is beyond our real comprehension (\"the more you know, the more you realize that you don't know\")."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 4
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Each generation will praise Your actions to the next generation;"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 5
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "and will tell them of Your (miraculous) mighty deeds (that they experienced)."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 5
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "I will discuss (with everyone) the beauty of Your natural world;"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 6
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "as well as speak of Your wonders (which are beyond our comprehension)."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 6
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(Says David HaMelech:) Others (are impressed by and) speak of Your miraculous wonders;"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 7
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "but I speak of Your constant chessed and daily greatness (which is no less miraculous)!"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 7
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "They (one generation passing down the heritage to the next) will speak of Your abundant goodness (notwithstanding whatever difficulties that generation may have endured);"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 8
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "and they sing about Your generosity (that Hashem blesses us with more than the strict letter of the law would dictate)."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 8
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Hashem is gracious (giving us goodness more than we deserve) and merciful; (and that is apparent in the fact that He is)"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 9
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "slow to anger, and thus shows His true greatness through His abundant chessed."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 9
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Hashem is good to all (of humanity—even those who have not yet lived up to their potential);"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 10
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "and His mercy extends to all that He has created (even the smallest of the animal world)."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 10
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "All of Your creations will thank You (for Your goodness); but Your righteous ones (who have used their God-given gifts to increase sanctity and goodness into the world) will draw increased energy from You, the Source of all blessing, and in turn (by their good deeds) they will increase blessing in Your world."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 11
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "They (Your righteous ones) will discuss the glory of Your Kingdom (the Hand of Hashem as seen in the beauty and complexity of the natural world—which we take for granted, and therefore must be discussed a lot); וּגְבוּרָתְךָ יְדַבֵּרוּ—and they will also tell of Your mighty open miracles (which are clear and do not need much discussion)."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 12
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "But when they speak to the common man, first they tell about Hashem's might and open miracles (since that is easy for people to see); וּכְבוֹד הֲדַר מַלְכוּתוֹ—and (from the open miracles they) then explain to the common people how to see the Hand of Hashem in the daily miracles of \"nature.\""
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 13
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Your Kingship is over all the \"worlds\" (the multitude of spiritual spheres and worlds that are beyond our comprehension); and וּמֶמְשַׁלְתְּךָ בְּכָל דּוֹר וָדֹר—Your Rulership spans eternity and governs each unique generation (in its own special role in Your master plan, all of which is also beyond our human comprehension)."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 14
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(Though Hashem is \"busy\" ruling over the entire universe and eternity, yet still He looks after each and) He supports every individual who has fallen (spiritually or emotionally); וְזוֹקֵף לְכָל הַכְּפוּפִים—and He helps every person who is bent over (from his struggles) to get up (and continue his climb toward personal perfection)."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 15
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(Therefore) every creature, from the smallest to the greatest, looks to You with hope (that You will take care of them);"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "and You do give each one its (physical, spiritual, and emotional) sustenance—just at the time they really need it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(Thus we proclaim emphatically that) You open Your Hand;"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "and give each person what they need in order to be satisfied. (If you feel you are not getting what you need—focus on the next verse…)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "All that Hashem does is just and righteous (even though as humans it does not always appear that way to us);"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "and He applies that justice with great kindness."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(In truth,) Hashem is close to all who call to Him;"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "but one must call out to Hashem with emes—honesty and sincerity. (This means that (1) you do not say one thing in your tefillos but then by your actions distance yourself from Hashem; (2) in general, whenever you speak it is with honesty, i.e., you are a \"man of your word\" and sincere; and (3) it is clear from your actions that you are sincere in your requests from Hashem, since you are doing whatever you personally can do to achieve those goals.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "He fulfills the will of those who fear Him;"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "and He hears their cries (in times of trouble) and He saves them. (That is for those who serve Hashem from fear [מיראה].)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(But) those who serve Hashem from love (מאהבה), He will protect them from troubles"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "in the first place! (Alternatively,) for those who serve Hashem from love (מֵאַהֲבָה), He reserves and preserves (שׁוֹמֵר) their ultimate and eternal reward to be given in Olam Haba;"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "and Hashem will destroy all evil."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "May my mouth declare the praises of Hashem (so powerfully and sincerely, that);"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 22
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "everyone (will be so impacted by my words and actions, that they too) will bless Hashem and see Him as the Source for all blessings—for eternity!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "And each of us (in our way, based on our own life experiences,) will thank Hashem and see Him as the Source of blessing in our individual lives;"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 23
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "now and forever (no matter what will happen! To sum it all up in one word:);"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 23
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "whatever happens, praise Hashem!"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 4
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(The chazzan proclaims our hope that) soon, in our lifetime, the entire world, which Hashem created precisely according to His Will, will recognize Hashem as the Source of all and will see the sanctity, perfection, and purpose of all He has done."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 24
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(We all enthusiastically respond:) Absolutely correct! May everyone (including me!), everywhere, and forever, see that all His actions are great and deserving of praise!"
            }
