    {
      "kind": "instant_insight",
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "It does not say that Hashem picks up the \"נֹפְלִים\" — those who have fallen, rather He is \"סוֹמֵךְ\" — He supports them. Why doesn't Hashem simply pick us up? Because falling is part of the growth process, as Shlomo HaMelech (Mishlei 24:16) tells us, \"The tzaddik falls down seven times and gets up.\" The energy involved in getting back up is needed to build our \"spiritual muscles,\" and therefore we must do that on our own. But He does support and help us!"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "instant_insight",
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "It does not say that Hashem gives \"mazon\" — sustenance. Rather it says that He gives \"ratzon,\" which literally means He gives us \"desire\" or the \"will\" to accomplish. Sometimes, when we are down, what we need is not more stuff but rather, an infusion of the will and energy to push forward and move onward and upward."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
